{"type":"text","timestamp":1788213283076,"sessionID":"ses_fa630cc01ffefTEin5wfy7Iwv6","part":{"id":"prt_059d13822001rYso2ge6lzOuHP","messageID":"msg_059d12f5e001HlfyprWf3IKHF3","sessionID":"ses_fa630cc01ffefTEin5wfy7Iwv6","type":"text","text":"Implemented the fix in `flakyqueue/scheduler.py` and wrote the report to `/workspace/out/root_cause.md`.\n\nWhat changed:\n- `Scheduler.add()` now uses the injected clock instead of `time.time()`.\n- `Scheduler.ready()` now uses the injected clock and a deterministic sort order instead of `random.shuffle(...)`.\n- `Scheduler.schedule_retry()` now uses the injected random source and injected clock, while keeping retry jitter.\n\nDeterministic ordering is now:\n- higher `priority` first\n- earlier `run_at`\n- earlier `created_at`\n- lexical `id` as the final tie-breaker\n\nVerification:\n- Attempted `python -m pytest tests`, but this container has no `python` binary.\n- Attempted `python3 -m pytest tests`, but `pytest` is not installed and this environment also lacks `pip`/`ensurepip`/working `venv` bootstrap.\n- Manually invoked the test functions under `tests/` with `python3`; they passed.\n- Ran an additional direct determinism check; it passed.\n\nFiles changed:\n- `/workspace/in/flakyqueue/flakyqueue/scheduler.py`\n- `/workspace/out/root_cause.md`","time":{"start":1788213278754,"end":1788213283072},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0154a1ba9f2bf9ee016a95f81eada487d2b251bdcbd731e0c3","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
